---
import DocsLayout from '../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
import Callout from '../components/Callout.astro';
import Toc from '../components/Toc.astro';
import { withBase } from '../lib/paths';

const toc = [
	{id: 'binaries', label: 'Binaries'},
	{id: 'modes', label: 'Modes'},
	{id: 'flags', label: 'Flags & files'},
	{id: 'contract-id', label: 'Contract ID'},
	{id: 'exit', label: 'Exit codes'},
	{id: 'errors', label: 'Error messages'},
	{id: 'stdout', label: 'Stdout summary'},
	{id: 'network', label: 'Network'},
];
---

<DocsLayout
	title="CLI reference"
	eyebrow="[ 08 · CLI ]"
	description="Headless and interactive entry points — same audit engine, explicit exit semantics for CI."
>
	<Toc items={toc} />

	<h2 id="binaries">Binaries</h2>
	<table>
		<thead>
			<tr>
				<th>Command</th>
				<th>Entry</th>
				<th>Purpose</th>
			</tr>
		</thead>
		<tbody>
			<tr>
				<td><code>kuyfi</code></td>
				<td><code>dist/cli.js</code></td>
				<td>TUI (no args) or headless audit (Contract ID)</td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<td><code>kuyfi-server</code></td>
				<td><code>dist/server.js</code></td>
				<td>Paid OSINT HTTP API — see <a href={withBase('/paid-api')}>Paid scan API</a></td>
			</tr>
		</tbody>
	</table>

	<h2 id="modes">Modes</h2>
	<p>
		<code>cli.tsx</code> uses <code>meow</code> + <code>selectCliMode()</code> in
		<code>cli_runtime.ts</code>:
	</p>
	<table>
		<thead>
			<tr>
				<th>Mode</th>
				<th>When</th>
				<th>Behavior</th>
			</tr>
		</thead>
		<tbody>
			<tr>
				<td><code>tui</code></td>
				<td>No positional args</td>
				<td>Interactive Ink TUI</td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<td><code>headless</code></td>
				<td>Valid Contract ID</td>
				<td><code>runHeadlessAudit()</code> — full OSINT + Chaos Monkey</td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<td><code>invalid</code></td>
				<td>Positional arg that fails the ID regex</td>
				<td>Prints expected shape; exits <code>1</code></td>
			</tr>
		</tbody>
	</table>

	<pre><code># Interactive TUI
kuyfi

# Headless audit (stdout summary only)
kuyfi &lt;CONTRACT_ID&gt;

# Headless + exports
kuyfi &lt;CONTRACT_ID&gt; --json
kuyfi &lt;CONTRACT_ID&gt; --pdf
kuyfi &lt;CONTRACT_ID&gt; --json --pdf

# From source checkout
npm start
node dist/cli.js &lt;CONTRACT_ID&gt; --json</code></pre>

	<h2 id="flags">Flags &amp; file names</h2>
	<p>v0.1.0 exposes exactly two flags — no verbosity, timeout, or network selector:</p>
	<table>
		<thead>
			<tr>
				<th>Flag</th>
				<th>Writes</th>
				<th>Default filename</th>
			</tr>
		</thead>
		<tbody>
			<tr>
				<td><code>--json</code></td>
				<td>SecurityReport JSON</td>
				<td><code>kuyfi-report-&lt;reportId&gt;.json</code></td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<td><code>--pdf</code></td>
				<td>SecurityReport PDF</td>
				<td><code>kuyfi-report-&lt;reportId&gt;.pdf</code></td>
			</tr>
		</tbody>
	</table>

	<ul>
		<li>
			When both flags are set, <code>buildSecurityReport()</code> runs <strong>once</strong>
			— JSON and PDF share the same <code>reportId</code> / findings.
		</li>
		<li>
			Writes use <code>flag: 'wx'</code> — never silent overwrite. Collision →
			<code>Refusing to overwrite existing file: …</code> and exit <code>1</code>.
		</li>
		<li>
			If JSON succeeds and PDF then fails (or vice versa), the process still exits
			<code>1</code>; the successful path is still reported when available.
		</li>
	</ul>

	<h2 id="contract-id">Contract ID shape</h2>
	<pre><code>/^C[A-Z0-9]&#123;55&#125;$/
# Exactly 56 characters: C + 55 uppercase A–Z / 0–9 (no lowercase)</code></pre>
	<p>
		Invalid ID message: <code>Expected 56 characters starting with C (A-Z, 0-9)</code>.
	</p>

	<h2 id="exit">Exit codes</h2>
	<table>
		<thead>
			<tr>
				<th>Code</th>
				<th>Meaning</th>
			</tr>
		</thead>
		<tbody>
			<tr>
				<td><code>0</code></td>
				<td>
					Audit completed (scan + Chaos Monkey finished). <strong>Independent of
					finding severity</strong> — CRITICAL findings still exit 0.
				</td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<td><code>1</code></td>
				<td>
					Tool failure: invalid Contract ID, <code>ScanError</code>, Chaos Monkey
					internal throw, or export I/O (including EEXIST overwrite refusal).
				</td>
			</tr>
		</tbody>
	</table>

	<Callout type="warn" title="CI pitfall">
		<p>
			Do <strong>not</strong> treat exit code as “vulnerabilities found.” Parse the
			JSON report (<code>summary</code> / <code>findings</code>) for severity gates.
			See <a href={withBase('/reports')}>Reports</a>.
		</p>
	</Callout>

	<h2 id="errors">Error messages (<code>describeAuditError</code>)</h2>
	<table>
		<thead>
			<tr>
				<th>Source</th>
				<th>CLI text</th>
			</tr>
		</thead>
		<tbody>
			<tr>
				<td><code>CONTRACT_NOT_FOUND</code></td>
				<td>Contract not found on Testnet. Check the Contract ID.</td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<td><code>XDR_ALIGN_FAILURE</code></td>
				<td>Could not parse the contract spec (contractspecv0 section missing or invalid).</td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<td><code>RPC_UNAVAILABLE</code></td>
				<td>Soroban Testnet RPC is unreachable.</td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<td><code>UNKNOWN</code> ScanError</td>
				<td><code>Scan failed: &lt;message&gt;</code></td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<td>Other thrown Error</td>
				<td><code>Audit failed: &lt;message&gt;</code></td>
			</tr>
		</tbody>
	</table>

	<h2 id="stdout">Stdout summary</h2>
	<p>
		On a successful headless run, stdout starts with
		<code>formatAuditSummary()</code>:
	</p>
	<pre><code>KUYFI AUDIT COMPLETE

Contract: C…
Network: TESTNET
Functions scanned: N
Vectors executed: N
Findings: N
  Critical / High / Medium / Low / Info: …

Evidence:
  Broadcast transactions: N
  Transactions with hash: N</code></pre>
	<p>
		Progress during the run comes from <code>onProgress</code> in <code>audit.ts</code>
		(e.g. scanning / Chaos Monkey stage lines). With <code>--json</code> /
		<code>--pdf</code>, successful paths append
		<code>JSON report written to: …</code> / <code>PDF report written to: …</code>.
	</p>

	<h2 id="network">Network</h2>
	<p>
		RPC URL is a single constant in <code>network.ts</code>:
		<code>https://soroban-testnet.stellar.org</code>. No mainnet selector, no
		<code>--rpc</code> flag in v0.1.0.
	</p>
</DocsLayout>
